<<<
+ ratio is four times as high for amongst as for among; though the total number of quotations is too small to justify the belief that this proportion prevails generally, it probably indicates a tendency. It may be said with some confidence that (1) among is the normal word, (2) amongst is more usual before vowels, but (3) before the, which so commonly follows as easily to outnumber all other initials, the two forms are used quite indifferently.
===
+ ratio is four times as high for *amongst* as for *among*; though the total number of quotations is too small to justify the belief that this proportion prevails generally, it probably indicates a tendency. It may be said with some confidence that (1) *among* is the normal word, (2) *amongst* is more usual before vowels, but (3) before *the*, which so commonly follows as easily to outnumber all other initials, the two forms are used quite indifferently.
>>>

