<<<
amour. Being established in English, & not likely ever to be expelled, it is better pronounced with the normal English accent (&’moor). Retention of a foreign accent undoubtedly discourages the popular use of a word, & if the word is worth having at all this is very undesirable. See FRENCH PRONUNCIATION.
===
**amour.** Being established in English, & not likely ever to be expelled, it is better pronounced with the normal English accent (ă'moor). Retention of a foreign accent undoubtedly discourages the popular use of a word, & if the word is worth having at all this is very undesirable. See ^^FRENCH PRONUNCIATION^^.
>>>

